{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/476104-freeze-the-descent","id":476104,"title":"Freeze the Descent?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-10T11:13:36-07:00","id":476104,"title":"Freeze the Descent?","content":"Is possible trought a ritual, curse or something else to freeze the sekhem drop? I were thinking about the case of a big bad guy sealed somewhere for decades but still conscious.... something like Baal in Diablo 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T11:17:52-07:00","id":476122,"title":"","content":"I'll answer according to NWoD Protocol:<br /> <br /> &quot;Not in the books as such, but nothing stopping you from doing that in your games if that's what you want.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T12:22:13-07:00","id":476196,"title":"","content":"There's that one Affinity that lets you sleep, freezing your Sekhem until awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T18:31:43-07:00","id":476484,"title":"","content":"One of the possible cenarios of the Rite of Irem Reborn in D.C was to stop Sekhem from dropping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T23:41:32-07:00","id":476717,"title":"","content":"The Avarice Chronicle (part 1 in <i>Guildhalls</i>) had a relic sarcophagus which rapidly dropped a mummy to Sekhem 1, and kept them there in a coma-like state. <br /> <br /> If you were going to create your own power to handle it, I'd probably recommend designing a high level Seba; that seems along the lines of some of the cosmic relics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T23:47:46-07:00","id":476718,"title":"","content":"Who needs anything? Maybe he really has just eked out an existence at Sekhem 1 from the first Sothic turn and he seriously just never died","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T08:44:45-07:00","id":477010,"title":"","content":"That depends, how morale do you want it to be?<br /> <br /> Because the bane affinity ammut's feast allows you to reset your sekhem counter by eating hearts, in sothis ascends there's a group of mummies who halt their sekhem drop by having cults who sacrifice people to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:48:24-07:00","id":479261,"title":"","content":"It would be useful for the Judges to have their servants stay up and about, yet whatever means you end up using, they don't seem to be asking mummies to use them. Which implies that whatever those means are, it's something that is otherwise deleterious to the Judge's interests. The seba and bane power ideas both fit that bill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T18:27:16-07:00","id":496938,"title":"","content":"Not the same thing as halting the drop, but if you could snag enough mortal sorcerers and get them producing lots of relics you could probably ride that for a while. Assuming the judges didn't take too much umbrage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T18:42:33-07:00","id":496947,"title":"","content":"&quot;Lots&quot; of relics might be hard though, since most mortals only churn out one, maybe two or three relics in the course of a lifetime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T19:48:31-07:00","id":497010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/476104-freeze-the-descent?p=496947#post496947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Lots&quot; of relics might be hard though, since most mortals only churn out one, maybe two or three relics in the course of a lifetime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you could instruct them in the arts of lost Irem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T20:29:02-07:00","id":497034,"title":"","content":"I dunno. Mummies can't make relics anymore and are unlikely to remember arts they learned from their mortal lives. And then there's the fact that the Book of the Deceived seems to imply that the Rite of Return took something out of the world. It might not be possible to produce relics at that prodigious rate anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T20:37:01-07:00","id":497038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/476104-freeze-the-descent?p=497010#post497010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps you could instruct them in the arts of lost Irem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that it's been hinted several times that Mummies have lost the ability to create Relics, I doubt that could happen.<br /> <br /> However, given what has been so far, Iremic Relic creation apparently takes a lot out of Mortals. Either via time or simply chunks of their Soul. This and Mortal Sorcery really need a book...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T04:57:35-07:00","id":497322,"title":"","content":"Well if one wants more powerful sorcerers it was also suggested that perhaps the sorcerers capable of making more than a couple of relics were also powerful enough to avoid mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T05:32:10-07:00","id":497343,"title":"","content":"At the risk of sounding stupid, did the actual people of Irem create relics? I got the impression that it might have been the Shaniatu doing the magic and the guilds were basically cargo cults around them who helped out and did the mundane work of the empire. At the very least it seems that a lot of the Arisen weren't directly invovled in the creation of relics and therefore may not have ever known how they were created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T06:22:59-07:00","id":497372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/476104-freeze-the-descent?p=497343#post497343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of sounding stupid, did the actual people of Irem create relics? I got the impression that it might have been the Shaniatu doing the magic and the guilds were basically cargo cults around them who helped out and did the mundane work of the empire. At the very least it seems that a lot of the Arisen weren't directly invovled in the creation of relics and therefore may not have ever known how they were created.</div> </div> </div> </div>The actual people of Irem absolutely did create relics. In fact, I'd struggle to believe that there's a single Arisen who <i>didn't</i>. They were all Craftsmen chosen from the sacred Guildhalls by the Shan'iatu, and I don't see them picking ones with no affinity for relics. Remember that Kepher relies on an Arisen's sympathy to their Guild's relics in order to locate them, for example (although that admittedly gets a little wonky with Arisen who swap Guilds). The major perk of hitting Memory 6 is being able to remember every object you made with your own two hands. Then you have relics like Pyropus, presumably mass-produced by the Mesen-Nebu to outfit Irem's armies. Only the five dot Pyropus is stated to have been made by the Shan'iatu personally. Last but not least, it's stated several times (from Talisman rules to the details on Apotheosis) that one of the sources of great despair for Arisen, all Arisen, is that they have lost the power to manipulate Sekhem to craft relics in the ways they once did. As craftsmen who presumably took pride in their work, losing the ability to perform this generative act is quite painful for many of the Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T00:11:20-07:00","id":499937,"title":"","content":"Yes, I can't blame someone for being unsure, it did seem rather ambiguous at first, but things got more clear with later books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:15:52-07:00","id":585186,"title":"","content":"Does Sekhem go down while in a death cycle? The Core Book does say so explicitly, and almost implies that it does not. If so, one could just abstain from Resurrection and maintain a high Sekhem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:34:24-07:00","id":585204,"title":"","content":"I don't think you have any choice in whether you resurrect or not. There is a timer that indicates how long it takes for you to resurrect (dictated by a comparison of Sekhem and Memory), which is the length of your Death Cycle, and undergoing the Death Cycle makes it almost certain you will lose a dot of Sekhem, minimum. That very slim chance to the contrary, requiring an Exceptional Success on a Memory roll followed by no successes on a Descent check, could be why you think it implies that you don't lose Sekhem in the Death Cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:44:38-07:00","id":585473,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'm fairly certain that entering an Akhet is a conscious choice on the part of the Mummy. Far as I can tell, if a mummy is willing to remain in Twilight nothing forces them back into the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:48:04-07:00","id":585483,"title":"","content":"Do Akhets actually figure in the Death Cycle? The way they're sequestered off in a sidebar always made me think they were specific cases in which the Arisen physically ended up in Neter-Khetet (primarily through the Twilight Abduction Numen or the third tier of Kiss of Apep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T19:30:30-07:00","id":587611,"title":"","content":"If the reason for mortal sorcerers having low output is a problem of a weakening soul, maybe the answer is Mages? They're damn good with soul manipulation (especially the Tremere, but I doubt their helpfulness here), and so they could possibly help fuel increased output. Alternately, they might be able to make a Perfecting Fate/Prime/Life spell to slow the Descent or impose penalties to the Descent roll? I know, &quot;Mages horn in on everything&quot;, but I think it's a real and valid possibility. Give the Mages something to study in exchange for some help staying up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}